  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1240 PM CDT Thu Sep 10 2026\n\nA shortwave trough and associated frontal boundary currently \ntraversing the area has brought widespread rain showers to \ncentral and southeast Illinois through midday. Synoptic scale \nascent has weakened over the past few hours and this trend is \nexpected to continue, causing the showers to scatter out and \neventually diminish by early evening over southeast IL.\n\nSinking motion and surface high pressure building across the\nGreat Lakes will promote clearing skies tonight and Friday\nmorning. High temperatures on Friday rebound into the lower to \nmid 80s as broad southeasterly flow resumes. \n\nTwo low chances of rain develop for late Friday through\nSunday. The first is associated with a weak upper wave passing \nto our south, which could spread scattered showers as far north \nas southeast to east central IL Friday afternoon and Friday \nnight. Separately, a frontal boundary over the upper Midwest \nmakes some progress southeast on Saturday night into Sunday, \nand this brings low chance PoPs into the western CWA.\n\nHigh confidence resides in a substantial warming trend Saturday\nthrough Tuesday (Sep 12-15). An upper-level ridge amplifies \nacross the central to eastern CONUS, supported by strong \nagreement between deterministic and ensemble mean guidance. NBM\nblended guidance projects daily high temperatures climbing into\nthe upper 80s to lower 90s through this period. The ECMWF \nExtreme Forecast Index (EFI) highlights maximum temperature \nvalues ranging from 0.70 to 0.85 across central Illinois, \nindicating climatologically unusual warmth for mid- September. \nGuidance supports dew points generally in the 60s though this \nstretch, which would keep daily peak heat indices below 100 \ndegrees.\n\nThe next chance for appreciable rain holds off until some point\nnext week when the next cold front moves into the Midwest.\nThe guidance envelope shows a large spread in timing, which is\nexpected as the system is moving into a strong ridge. As a\nresult, NBM's chance to likely PoPs stretch through Mon-Thu.\nML/AI severe outlook produce show a low (5%) risk area centered\naround Tuesday.",
